#
# D-0279: a service account that no program could ever use.
#
# Owner ask, verbatim: "poi devi mettere una chat che possa parlare con coden evolution e
# noesar" -- a chat inside Debug Evolution that relays into this control plane. That relay
# needs a non-interactive credential, and this product already had one on paper: the
# `service_account` role, `userDirectory.issueServiceToken()`, and a complete, tested
# `authenticateServiceToken()`. What it did not have was a request path that ever called
# the verifier. `requireSession()` read the `noesar_session` cookie and nothing else, so a
# bearer token was rejected everywhere and the role was unusable by construction -- the
# same shape of defect as the update-channel key in D-0272, a finished verifier with no
# way in.
#
# Two changes, both in the authentication layer and nowhere else:
#
#  1. server.mjs -- `resolveAuthenticated()` tries the cookie FIRST and falls back to a
#     bearer service token. It returns a session-SHAPED object with `elevatedUntil:0`
#     rather than `session:null`, so the routes that demand recent strong reauthentication
#     answer 403 (the right answer for an account with no password and no TOTP) instead of
#     dereferencing null and answering 500. `requireCsrf()` short-circuits for that caller:
#     CSRF defends an AMBIENT credential, and a bearer token in an Authorization header is
#     never ambient -- the same reasoning already written down for SCIM.
#
#  2. auth.mjs -- the service-account permission set gains `workspace.write`, matching
#     `client_restricted` exactly. The narrower set looked safer than it was: `provider.use`
#     already writes, because chat/stream calls graph.addMessage twice per turn. The account
#     could append to a conversation but not create the conversation to append into, which
#     is self-contradictory rather than restrictive. It still cannot register a provider,
#     define an agent or a tool, or promote into shared memory.
#
# THIS IS A SECURITY-SURFACE CHANGE and is named as one: reverting it is a one-line edit in
# each file. Verified before this build: unit 1403/1404 (1 skipped, 0 failed -- the same
# figures as D-0278), ESLint 274 files 0 errors 0 warnings.
#
# Built FROM the current live tag: 12 overlay2 layers, far below the 128 limit that forced
# the flatten in D-0273.

FROM noesar-evolution:phase4-debug-evolution-tools

LABEL org.noesar.phase="4-service-token-auth"
LABEL org.noesar.feature="bearer-service-token-authentication-wired-into-requireSession"
LABEL org.noesar.base-image="noesar-evolution:phase4-debug-evolution-tools"

USER root
COPY --chown=10001:10001 services/reference-control-plane/ /opt/noesar/services/reference-control-plane/
USER 10001:10001
